[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] ## What shipped
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] **Photo audit first.** I opened all 11 photos before writing layout code and independently confirmed the brief's finding: `photo-7` (صالون كمال, with a "SINCE 1989" graphic), `photo-10` (صالون عايد), and `photo-11` (Gemini Barbershop, carrying their logo, two phone numbers, and social handles) are **other businesses**. They're not imported at all in `src/data/photos.ts`, so they can't reach a component — verified absent from `dist/`. Usable pool: 8, and every layout is sized to 8.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] **Layout devices** — asymmetric 58/42 hero with the real red awning in a `-3°` plate that bleeds off the inline-end and bottom edge (mirrored to `+3°` in RTL), an accent rule riding the plate's top edge continuing the awning line; a 12-column bento mosaic with the red 4.9/580 stat panel embedded among the craft photos; services as a numbered index-row list with a cursor-parked photo preview, not a card grid; `-3°` clip-path wedges between sections.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] **Signature moment** works and scrubs: at 25% through the pinned track the ring reads 363/3.1 partially drawn, at 62% it's 580/4.9 complete with the red flash and the craft lines wiped up.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] **Bugs I found and fixed via the live browser**, none of which the build would have caught:
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] - The letter-split wordmark rendered **"IWAKKAM"** in Arabic — RTL flex reversed the spans.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.505Z] - The service preview never appeared in Arabic — `inset-inline-start` anchored it to the right edge, so the JS translate pushed it off-screen. It's now deliberately physical `left`, with a comment saying why.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] - `::first-letter` drop-cap **tore Arabic words apart** (صالون → ص + الون). Arabic now gets its own editorial device.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] - Nav links overlapped at 1440px in English; the mobile hero plate sat under the CTAs; the hero duplicated "4.9"; alt text was hard-coded Arabic on the English page.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] **On the brief's "no Ali"** — the storefront alt originally transcribed "SALOON ALI MAKKAWI FOR MEN" from the sign. Since `facts.json` names no individual, I rewrote it to "a red awning carrying the shop name". No "Ali" anywhere in `dist/`.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] **Two deviations worth naming.** The brief forbids an embedded map (`lat`/`lng` are null), but the prompt's functional requirements mandate one "by address if coordinates are missing." I resolved this by querying the embed with the real Plus Code `XR5Q+P4 Amman` — a precise identifier from `facts.json`, not a fabricated coordinate — kept the decorative panel and Plus Code typography, and colour-graded the tiles into the palette. Second: the brief omitted the services section for lack of `menuOrServices`; per the prompt's override, seven category-standard offerings ship, with **no price, duration, or "from" figure** on any of them — the price slot is a WhatsApp chip with a service-specific prefilled message.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] **Verification:** clean build, no warnings. Zero console errors, page errors, or failed requests across ar/en × desktop/390px. No horizontal overflow at 390px. Every `scroll()` return is called as a plain function (never `.stop()`); the one `.finished` is on an `animate()` result; every `inView` observes a shared parent so groups animate once; no motion code in frontmatter; no bare imports in `is:inline` scripts. Reduced motion keeps the signature moment (track shortens 260svh → 130svh, numbers still resolve) and leaves nothing stuck hidden. No-JS still shows the full hero and all service rows. `dist/` has zero bare-root paths, valid JSON-LD in both languages, and `tel:+962796379479` / `wa.me/962796379479` / `mapsUrl` used as-is.
[2026-07-25T03:01:24.506Z] One thing to flag for you: `reviews` is empty, so there is no quote anywhere on the site — the trust story is carried entirely by the 4.9/580 numerals plus outbound links to the real Google reviews. If review text gets captured later, that section has room for it without restructuring.
